From a7866ddc520f0d66943c7fa16cc3c13627a4bc6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:27:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 38/41] [TSReader] Keep the segments of frames that can still
 come, and limit held audio by stream time

Round 11 finding (Sol): held audio pinned every later segment record.
Three audio frames without a PTS, then video only, kept 100 records
after 100 segments. The 1 s limit counted only the held audio, so
without more audio the frames waited up to the end of the stream.

Sol also showed a defect from before this range: a PES across more than
8 segments lost the PTS diff of the segment where the PES started,
because the reader kept the last 8 segments by count.

- MarkSegmentStart now keeps the new segment, the segments of held
  frames, and the segments of the PES in the buffers of each stream
  (ElementaryStream::AddPesSegments), and drops every other segment.
  MAX_SEGMENTS and the oldest-segment rule of 5b15574 are gone.
- Held audio now also comes without a PTS when the DTS of another
  stream is more than 1 s after the first DTS of that stream while the
  frames wait (wrap-aware, TSReader::IsPtsBefore). The reference starts
  again with the first frame of each new hold.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
